WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.460
Fans of "The Big Bang Theory" can point out plenty&nbsp;
of fun moments from the show's 12 seasons. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.960
that time Penny, played by Kaley Cuoco, gives&nbsp;
Jim Parsons’ Sheldon the ultimate Christmas gift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.120
to the scene in which Penny solves string theory,&nbsp;
it's hard to get any consensus on which of the CBS&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.680
sitcom's seasons viewers like the best, although&nbsp;
most seem to prefer the first six seasons.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.480
Naturally, the actors all have their own&nbsp;
favorite moments, and several of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.523
come in the Season 4 episode called "The&nbsp;
Agreement Dissection." Parsons told TBS,

00:00:29.523 --> 00:00:33.480
"I loved the structure of this episode,&nbsp;
the way I got to sort of take part in two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.060
different story lines: girls&nbsp;
night and the fight over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.960
roommate agreement at home. It was also&nbsp;
a really fun episode with Mayim Bialik."

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.000
And in a 2011 San Diego Comic-Con panel in&nbsp;
which the actors were asked about their favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.745
moments from Season 4, Bialik joked that a kiss&nbsp;
between her character, Amy, and Penny was hers.

00:00:50.745 --> 00:00:55.140
"I kissed a girl and I liked it."

00:00:56.563 --> 00:00:57.815
"What happened to you?"

00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:02.100
And then Bialik said more seriously that&nbsp;
the drunken kiss between Amy and Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.000
was really her favorite. Cuoco also&nbsp;
revealed her favorite moment as being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.900
from that episode since she had to convince&nbsp;
an actor to sexually harass her on-screen.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.500
Cuoco explained that the scene was&nbsp;
her favorite moment of Season 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.736
although it was hard for her&nbsp;
to pick just one. She said,

00:01:16.736 --> 00:01:18.960
"I guess it was where I had a lovely man have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.680
grab my ass in an episode when we were&nbsp;
dancing. And he was a little older man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.940
and he was so nervous. And it was so against&nbsp;
everything he believed in, and I was like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.200
'Honey, just grab it. Just do it.' And&nbsp;
he closed his eyes and just went for it."

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.860
In the episode, Sheldon crashes&nbsp;
a girls' night after lawyer Priya&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.940
basically nullifies the roommate agreement&nbsp;
he has with Leonard. When Amy, Penny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.380
and Bernadette discover that Sheldon can do&nbsp;
the cha-cha, rumba, and waltz, they decide to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.240
take him to a place they can waltz. At a dance&nbsp;
hall, an older man asks Bernadette to dance;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.040
when she says no, he asks Penny, and she&nbsp;
agrees. As he takes her out to the floor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.836
however, the man takes a certain liberty&nbsp;
until Penny slides his hand back into place.

00:01:57.836 --> 00:02:03.000
The man in question is Gabriel Tsai, an actor&nbsp;
who has just a few credits to his name. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.987
his part in "The Agreement Dissection"&nbsp;
is so small that it isn't one of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.987 --> 00:02:10.080
Wherever he is now, though, he&nbsp;
can say his tiny little role had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.558
an outsize effect on a favorite&nbsp;
episode of "The Big Bang Theory."

00:02:13.558 --> 00:02:18.240
Kaley Cuoco was happy to let an older man squeeze&nbsp;
her butt for the aforementioned scene. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.320
while she was clearly committed to the part,&nbsp;
she made sure that Penny was presented as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.980
more than an object for people's desires on&nbsp;
the later seasons of "The Big Bang Theory."

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:30.240
In an interview with W Magazine, Cuoco&nbsp;
said that she was happy for her character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.960
to be sexualized during the earlier&nbsp;
seasons of the sitcom. At the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.759
it made sense as Leonard and his&nbsp;
friends were crushing on her. She said,

00:02:37.759 --> 00:02:39.240
"I was the cute girl next door to the nerds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.780
right? It was all about booty&nbsp;
shorts and Juicy Couture zip-ups."

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.460
However, both Penny and Cuoco grew up as time&nbsp;
went on, and Cuoco wanted the character to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.420
shown in a different light to reflect that&nbsp;
— especially when it came to her outfits.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.360
"All of a sudden it's like, 'Can I&nbsp;
have a long sleeve shirt? How about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.009
a slack? How about a loafer? I never&nbsp;
wanna see that high heel ever again!'"

